    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d191">

                <pb facs="0264" n="998" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg998"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Butler to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-07-25"><hi rendition="#italic">July 25,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Reply of Mexican Government regarding Rowes not yet received. Have ascertained,
                    however, that extradition Chester will be refused upon the ground of his Mexican
                    nationality, but he will be tried here for stolen funds. Richard will be held
                    pending the arrival of extradition papers. This result in despite of
                    presentation your cabled opinion of the 19th. Can you urge extradition Chester
                    through Mexican minister at Washington?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Butler.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
